06817 #edb/ref 1061 3548 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106817 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b5b6259b-d42d-5bce-bbd7-530a36ded592" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106817 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105852 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107037 #edb/ref 1064 "The **power of product rule** states that if we want to raise the product $xy$ to some power $n$, we must raise each factor to the power $n$ and then multiply:\n\n$$\n(xy)^n=x^n y^n\n$$\n\nFor example,\n\n$$\n(xy)^4=x^4y^4.\n$$\n\nTo see why the power of product rule is true, let's take the above example and work it out again the long way, changing the order of factors in the multiplication. We get the same result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(xy)^{4} & = \\\\ (xy)(xy)(xy)(xy) & = \\\\ (x\\cdot x\\cdot x\\cdot x)(y\\cdot y\\cdot y\\cdot y) & = \\\\ {x}^{4}{y}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe power of product rule is just a shortcut for the process above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107037 #edb/ref 1065 1482 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107037 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7aabbc0f-a3ca-5f05-b6ae-d7551b16ae1a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107037 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110005 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186501587 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110005 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186501704 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110005 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186501742 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110005 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186501762 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110005 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186501886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110005 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110005 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110005 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186501587 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110005 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f75d50b2-6f5a-5bce-9e0b-522b9985c2e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110616 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110616 #edb/ref 1037 #